{"frame":{"request_id":"<sigma:1>","type":"control_request","request":{"subtype":"initialize","hooks":{"PreToolUse":[{"hookCallbackIds":["hook_0"]}],"PostCompact":[{"hookCallbackIds":["hook_1"]}]},"sdkMcpServers":["sigma"],"sdkMcpServerManifests":{"sigma":{"initializeResult":{"protocolVersion":"2025-11-25","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":true}},"serverInfo":{"name":"sigma","version":"1.0.0"}},"toolsListResult":{"tools":[{"name":"start_worker","description":"Starts a worker: an agent in a conversation of its own, which the user can open, watch and talk to, and which keeps working after your turn ends. Returns the worker's task name at once. Its final answer comes back through wait_worker, or as a message when you are not waiting.\nIf your task is `/root/task1` and you name a worker \"scout\", its task name is `/root/task1/scout`. You can call it `scout` or `/root/task1/scout`; other agents reach it by its full name.\nA worker runs on your provider unless you name another. Set `provider` and `model` only to what the user named, unchanged. The providers are script (a scripted model), claude (Claude Code), openai (ChatGPT), agy (Antigravity's agy). On your provider the worker has your tools. A worker starts from your message alone, with none of your history or instructions, so write a complete brief, when it runs on another provider or you run in a harness (Claude Code or agy); otherwise it starts with your history, unless `fork_turns` is \"none\". When you name no model, the worker uses the agent type's model if the provider supports it. Otherwise it uses your model on your provider or the destination's default on another provider.\nStart workers only when the user, or instructions such as AGENTS.md or a skill, ask for workers, delegation or parallel work.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"task_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name for the worker. Use lowercase letters, digits, and underscores