":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"target":{"type":"string","description":"The worker's task name, as start_worker returned it, or relative to yours."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The follow-up task."}},"required":["target","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"wait_worker","description":"Waits for your workers and returns what they sent: a finished worker's final answer, or a message from one. What it returns is not delivered to you again. Returns timed_out true when nothing arrives in time; call it again to keep waiting. Returns early, with nothing received, when the user sends new input.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"timeout_ms":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Timeout in milliseconds. Defaults to 30000, min 10000, max 3600000."}},"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"list_workers","description":"Lists the agents of your tree, you and the workers under you, each by task name with whether it is running, done, interrupted or failed. Optionally filtered by task-name prefix.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path_prefix":{"type":"string","description":"Task-name prefix, without a trailing slash. Omit to list them all."}},"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"stop_worker","description":"Stops a worker's current turn, if any, and returns its previous status. The worker stays available for messages and follow-up tasks.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"target":{"type":"string","description":"The worker's task name, as start_worker returned it, or relative to yours."}},"required":["target"],"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}}]}}},"appendSystemPrompt":"Workers. This session can start workers with the mcp__sigma__start_worker tool. A worker is an agent in a conversation of its own, which the user can open, watch and talk to. Every worker you start, on your provider too, starts from your message alone, with none of your history, so write a complete brief. Start a worker when the user asks for one, or names a model or a provider for part of the work. Pass the provider and model they named, unchanged, in `provider` and `model`. When they name several, start one worker for each. With none named, leave `provider` out and the worker runs on your own models. For a quick helper inside your own turn, use your own subagent tool if you have one, or do the work yourself.","title":"Use the Agent tool with run_in_background set to true to start a general-purpose subagent, and give it this task in its own words: begin a long command in the background and come back at once. Do not run any command yourself, and do not wait for the subagent. Reply with exactly: started"}},"type":"expect_outbound"}
